        "title_top": "",
        "title": "Expert Backed Review Summary",
        "text": "<p>The TP-Link Deco BE63 brings next-generation Wi-Fi 7 technology to modern households that demand reliable connectivity across numerous devices. Its <strong>tri-band BE10000 architecture</strong> delivers theoretical wireless speeds of up to 5,188 Mbps on 6 GHz, 4,324 Mbps on 5 GHz, and 574 Mbps on 2.4 GHz. Wi-Fi 7 features such as Multi-Link Operation (MLO), 320 MHz channel bandwidth, and 4K-QAM help improve throughput and responsiveness when paired with compatible devices. The 6 GHz band offers additional spectrum that can reduce congestion, while intelligent mesh technology helps devices maintain stable connections as users move between rooms. Each Deco BE63 unit includes <strong>four 2.5 Gbps WAN/LAN Ethernet ports and a USB port</strong>, providing flexible connectivity for multi-gig internet plans, gaming consoles, and wired networking equipment. Setup is guided through the TP-Link Deco app, which also provides network monitoring, device management, guest Wi-Fi, and parental controls. TP-Link HomeShield adds security features, although certain advanced protections require a subscription. The system supports backward compatibility with older Wi-Fi devices and can be expanded using other compatible Deco units. However, advertised wireless speeds represent combined theoretical maximums rather than speeds achievable by a single device. Overall, the Deco BE63 is a strong option for upgrading busy households to faster, more flexible mesh networking.</p>",
        "body_align": "center",
        "content_width": "narrow",
        "align-heading": "center",
